<%
local error_descriptions = {
	rate_limit = "The request exceeded a request-rate or provider quota limit.",
	concurrency_limit = "The user's concurrent request limit was reached.",
	timeout = "The upstream request exceeded its deadline.",
	auth = "The selected provider rejected authentication or authorization.",
	client_disconnected = "The downstream client disconnected before completion.",
	model_not_found = "The requested model was unavailable or not granted to this user.",
	unsupported_protocol = "The selected model does not support this endpoint protocol.",
	invalid_request = "The request was rejected as invalid.",
	upstream_unavailable = "The selected provider was unavailable.",
	upstream_error = "The selected provider returned an error.",
	internal_error = "The router could not complete the request.",
}
%>
<form class="filters request-filters" method="get" action="/admin/requests" aria-label="Filter requests">
<label>User<input name="user" list="request-users" value="<%= filters.user or '' %>" maxlength="193" placeholder="Any user" autocomplete="off"></label>
<label>Channel<input name="channel" list="request-channels" value="<%= filters.channel or '' %>" maxlength="193" placeholder="Any channel" autocomplete="off"></label>
<label>Model<input name="model" list="request-models" value="<%= filters.model or '' %>" maxlength="193" placeholder="channel/model or alias" autocomplete="off"></label>
<label>Result<select name="outcome">
<option value="">All results</option>
<option value="success"<% if filters.outcome == "success" then %> selected<% end %>>Success</option>
<option value="error"<% if filters.outcome == "error" then %> selected<% end %>>Error</option>
</select></label><button type="submit">Apply filters</button> <a href="/admin/requests">Reset all</a>
<% for _, entry in ipairs({{"users", "user"}, {"channels", "channel"}, {"models", "model"}}) do %>
<datalist id="request-<%= entry[1] %>"><% for _, value in ipairs(options[entry[2]]) do %><option value="<%= value %>"></option><% end %></datalist>
<% end %>
</form>
<p class="muted filter-help">Exact matches. Suggestions include up to 100 names per field from retained history, including renamed or deleted entries; you can type any full name. Applying or removing a filter starts at its latest results.</p>
<% if #active_filters > 0 then %><nav class="filter-chips" aria-label="Active filters"><% for _, filter in ipairs(active_filters) do %><a href="<%= filter.remove_url %>" aria-label="Remove <%= filter.label %> filter: <%= filter.value %>"><span><%= filter.label %>: <strong><%= filter.value %></strong></span><span aria-hidden="true">×</span></a><% end %></nav><% end %>
<div class="section-heading request-heading"><div><h2><%= filters.before and "Older results" or "Latest requests" %></h2><p class="muted">Showing <%= #rows %> completed requests · up to <%= page_size %> per page.</p></div>
<nav class="request-pagination" aria-label="Request pages"><a href="<%= latest_url %>">Latest</a><% if older_url then %><a href="<%= older_url %>">Older →</a><% end %></nav></div>
<p class="muted filter-help">Last <%= retention_days %> days, up to <%= max_rows %> entries. Completion-order IDs, newest first; timestamps show request start in the server timezone. No prompts, responses or raw error messages are stored.</p>
<div class="scroll request-table" role="region" aria-label="Request history" tabindex="0"><table>
<thead><tr><th scope="col">ID</th><th scope="col">Started</th><th scope="col">User</th><th scope="col">Channel</th><th scope="col">Model</th><th scope="col">Protocol</th><th scope="col">Result</th><th scope="col">Duration</th><th scope="col">TTFT</th><th scope="col">Tokens/s</th><th scope="col">Input</th><th scope="col">Cached input</th><th scope="col">Output</th></tr></thead>
<tbody><% for _, row in ipairs(rows) do %>
<tr><td><%= row.id %></td><td class="request-time"><%= os.date("%Y-%m-%d %H:%M:%S", row.created_at) %></td>
<td><%= row.user %></td><td><%= row.channel ~= "" and row.channel or "—" %></td>
<td><span title="<%= row.model %>"><%= row.model:match("^[%w._%-]+/(.+)$") or (row.model ~= "" and row.model or "—") %></span>
<% if row.upstream_model ~= "" and row.upstream_model ~= row.model and row.model ~= row.channel .. "/" .. row.upstream_model then %>
<div class="muted">→ <%= row.upstream_model %></div>
<% end %></td>
<td><%= row.protocol == "responses" and "Responses" or "Chat Completions" %> · <%= row.stream and "SSE" or "JSON" %></td>
<td><span class="badge <%= row.status >= 400 and 'error' or 'ok' %>"><%= row.status %></span><% if row.error_code or row.status >= 400 then %><div class="muted" title="<%= error_descriptions[row.error_code] or 'No detailed category recorded. Raw upstream errors are not stored.' %>"><%= row.error_code or "Not recorded" %></div><% end %></td>
<td class="request-duration"><%= string.format("%.3fs", row.duration_ms / 1000) %></td>
<td><%= row.ttft_ms and string.format("%.3fs", row.ttft_ms / 1000) or "—" %></td>
<td><%= row.output_tps and string.format("%.1f", row.output_tps) or "—" %></td>
<% for _, key in ipairs({"input_tokens", "cached_input_tokens", "output_tokens"}) do %><td><%= row.estimated and "~" or "" %><%= row[key] %><% if key == "cached_input_tokens" then %> <span class="muted">(<%= row.input_tokens > 0 and ((row.estimated and "~" or "") .. string.format("%.1f%%", row.cached_input_tokens / row.input_tokens * 100)) or "—" %>)</span><% end %></td><% end %>
</tr>
<% end %>
<% if #rows == 0 then %><tr><td colspan="13"><div class="request-empty"><h3>No requests found.</h3><p class="muted">Try fewer filters or return to the latest matching results. Older entries may have expired.</p><a href="<%= latest_url %>">Latest matching results</a> · <a href="/admin/requests">Clear all filters</a></div></td></tr><% end %>
</tbody></table></div>
<nav class="request-pagination request-pagination-bottom" aria-label="Request pages, bottom"><a href="<%= latest_url %>">Latest</a><% if older_url then %><a href="<%= older_url %>">Older →</a><% end %></nav>
<details class="request-help"><summary>How to read these metrics</summary>
<p>Result is the logical outcome: stream failures may show 502 after HTTP 200; disconnected clients show 499. Token counts prefixed with ~ are estimates; cache tokens are included in input. Duration covers the full request, including streaming.</p>
<p>TTFT measures time from request handling to the first nonempty streamed text, reasoning or tool output, not headers or lifecycle events. Generation interval runs from first output until the provider call returns. Tokens/s is reported output tokens divided by this interval, including relay delays; it is not pure model decoding speed. JSON responses, old entries, streams without output, missing usage and failed requests have no speed value. Old rows may have no recorded error category.</p>
</details>
